Title:
PoolParty — Process Injection Using Windows Thread Pools (SafeBreach Labs)

Type:
Documentation / Course Module Series (with associated GitHub Tool + Blog + Conference Talk)

Short Summary (4-8 sentences max):
PoolParty is a set of eight novel process injection techniques that execute payloads by abusing Windows user-mode thread pool internals rather than creating remote threads or obvious APC patterns. It focuses on how TP_WORK/TP_TIMER/TP_WAIT/TP_IO/TP_JOB/TP_DIRECT and worker factory mechanisms can be manipulated so the target process’s existing worker threads dispatch attacker-controlled callbacks. The material covers thread pool architecture and internals (e.g., TppWorkerThread lifecycle, task queues, timer queues) and shows multiple variants including StartRoutine hijacking via NtSetInformationWorkerFactory and IOCP-based triggering via NtSetIoCompletion/NtSetIoCompletionEx. It also summarizes EDR bypass results presented at Black Hat EU 2023 and discusses detection ideas (notably IOCP/thread-pool–centric telemetry) and defensive recommendations. Useful primarily for red teamers, pentesters, and malware researchers building stealthier injection chains, and for blue teams designing detections around thread pool and worker factory abuse. Interesting because it shifts injection from well-monitored primitives to less commonly instrumented thread pool execution paths.

Technical Focus:
- Windows thread pool internals (TP_POOL, TP_WORK, TP_TIMER, TP_WAIT, TP_IO, TP_JOB, TP_DIRECT)
- Worker Factory objects and StartRoutine hijacking (NtSetInformationWorkerFactory)
- IOCP-based execution and completion packet abuse (NtSetIoCompletion, NtSetIoCompletionEx)
- ALPC-related thread pool abuse (TP_ALPC)
- Callback dispatch mechanics (TppWorkerThread, queue insertion, timer arming)
- Detection strategies for thread pool/IOCP anomalies

Use Cases:
- Stealth process injection without CreateRemoteThread-style artifacts
- Building EDR-evasive execution chains leveraging existing worker threads
- Researching Windows thread pool/worker factory attack surface and primitives
- Developing defensive detections around thread pool queue/timer/IOCP manipulation
- Training material for understanding modern injection tradecraft and mitigations

Keywords:
PoolParty, SafeBreach Labs, Alon Leviev, process injection, Windows thread pool, TP_POOL, TP_WORK, TP_TIMER, TP_WAIT, TP_IO, TP_JOB, TP_DIRECT, worker factory, NtSetInformationWorkerFactory, TppWorkerThread, I/O completion ports, IOCP, NtSetIoCompletion, NtSetIoCompletionEx, ALPC, EDR bypass, Black Hat EU 2023